Subject: Reordering bars by multiple variables
Message-ID: <srOY12BfxFw.SnizSzv6BQAJ@ggplot2.groups.google.com>
Archived-At: <https://groups.google.com/g/ggplot2/c/srOY12BfxFw/m/SnizSzv6BQAJ>
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset="utf-8"
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Say, I want to rearrange the bars in my plot by a variable, I can do something like

y = reorder(name, variable1)

But how would I go about using two variables for reordering? To first order by variable1, then by variable2?

From u3ada5bc98608b5f2 at groups.google.com  Mon Dec 18 01:53:22 2017
From: u3ada5bc98608b5f2 at groups.google.com (jyr...@gmail.com)
Date: Mon, 18 Dec 2017 01:53:22 +0000
Subject: Re: Reordering bars by multiple variables
Message-ID: <srOY12BfxFw.Bqc8PN36BQAJ@ggplot2.groups.google.com>
In-Reply-To: <srOY12BfxFw.SnizSzv6BQAJ@ggplot2.groups.google.com>
References: <srOY12BfxFw.SnizSzv6BQAJ@ggplot2.groups.google.com>
Archived-At: <https://groups.google.com/g/ggplot2/c/srOY12BfxFw/m/Bqc8PN36BQAJ>
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset="utf-8"
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Turns out this does the job:

y = reorder(reorder(name, variable2), variable1)

Not the prettiest looking solution but it works.

